 "pdf": "ads8556.pdf",
 "pages": "p.3-7 (pin functions), p.8 (ROC: BVDD 2.7-3.6 V / 4.5-5.5 V), p.14 (serial timing: tCONV, tD2 12 ns, tD3 15 ns, tD4 10 ns), p.15 (Figure 2: FS low drives the MSB, SDO changes on SCLK rising, SDI latched on SCLK falling), p.27-28 (Table 2, serial interface, Figure 37, Table 3 twos complement, software mode), p.30 (RESET, STBY), p.32-34 (CR, Figure 42, Table 5)",
 "notModeled": [
  "only the serial interface in software mode is modeled (PAR/SER = 1, HW/SW = 1, SEL_A = 1, SEL_B = SEL_C = 0: all six results on SDO_A in the order CH_A0, CH_A1, CH_B0, CH_B1, CH_C0, CH_C1, six 16-bit words with two leading zeros, 96 SCLKs); the PAR/SER, HW/SW, SEL_x, WORD/BYTE and DCEN straps are not read",
  "parallel interface (DB15-DB0 word or DB15-DB8 byte mode with CS/RD/WR, CR written in two 16-bit or four 8-bit writes): not modeled; the DB pins other than SDO_A are never driven",
  "hardware mode (separate CONVST_A/B/C starts, RANGE and REFEN pins, CR bits C[31:24] disregarded): not modeled; conversion starts on CONVST_A rising for all channels; CONVST_B/CONVST_C (sequential mode, SEQ with external XCLK) not modeled",
  "SDO_B and SDO_C outputs (two- or three-port read-out) and daisy-chain inputs DCIN_A/B/C: not modeled",
  "channel pair enables CH_A/B/C, power-down PD_x, auto-NAP, RANGE_x, REFEN, REFBUF, VREF, REFDAC, CLKSEL/CLKOUT_EN (external conversion clock XCLK): stored only; the output always carries six results of the 0 V code",
  "BUSY/INT polarity: the CR table (C20) says BUSY active high pairs with INT active low (default) and C20 = 1 gives BUSY active low / INT active high; the pin table says INT transitions high after a conversion completes. The CR table is modeled. In sequential mode BUSY pulses for one conversion clock per pair: not modeled",
  "READ_EN: the CR is shifted out once at the start of the next frame (32 bits) and READ_EN stays set in the register until rewritten; whether the device clears it is not stated",
  "STBY (standby: everything but the digital interface powered down, 10 ms wake-up) not modeled; RESET minimum 50 ns pulse; power-on reset behavior of AVDD",
  "SPI mode: SCLK idle level not specified (Figure 2 dashed); MSB is valid at FS fall, SDO changes on SCLK rising and SDI is latched on SCLK falling: modeled as mode 2",
  "analog inputs, ranges, reference DAC and acquisition time; maximum SCLK 36 MHz"
 ],
